<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60270" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρύφ-ιος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>IT</u>
			1328
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Th.
			7.25
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hidden,
				concealed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					1.84
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄφις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1328
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>secret, clandestine</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀαρισμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					789
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					360
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐναί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					719
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρωτες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Musae.
					1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψᾶφοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					8.26
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. εἰσῆλθον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>HF</u>
					598
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίως</span> Ps.- <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Philopatr.</u>
				9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>occult</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>Inst.</u>
				121
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				151
			</span></i>; <i>latent</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				192
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				201
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίως</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				153
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> voc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρύφιε</span>
			<i>such an one</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ru.</u>
				4.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρύφιος, ὁ</span>, fabulous gem, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Fluv.</u>
				13.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>6.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρύφιος, ὁ</span>, title of a grade of initiates in the mysteries
			of Mithras, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIL</u>
				6.751a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				753
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
